Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-30-2001||11:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jake_2m4:<BR><B>I mentioned getting a rebuilt 4cyl, and someone mentioned using a later version.  IE 1990 pontiac 6000, bc of better hp, cam, etc.  Would that require a new ECM or can I hook it up to my 85 set up like the original engine.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You will need the 6000 ECM and marry it to the Fiero...<BR>If you are going to that trouble, put in a 3800...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-31-2001||08:42 PM||||It will not drop in without significant work.<P>87 and up 4 cylinder needs all the wiring and ecm that match it. Also needs correct throttle cruise and tranny cables. If AC will need to mess with the compressor as well. (87+ uses a serpent belt. not a V belt...)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
